.TH OMACHAT-CTL 1 "2026-10-28" "OmaChat"
.SH NAME
omachat-ctl \- control the local identity daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B omachat-ctl
[--socket PATH] COMMAND
.SH COMMANDS
status [--json], fingerprint [--qr],
identity show, identity generate, identity import NSEC, identity export,
identity bind, identity unbind,
hosted-claim-handle HANDLE, hosted-resolve-handle HANDLE,
chat-prepare, contacts-add PEER, contacts-list, contacts-remove NPUB,
relays-show, relays-set URL..., send PEER TEXT, messages.
Handle commands and identity show/generate/bind accept --json.
identity export prints the nsec. Nothing else prints that secret.
.SH PANIC
panic --confirm ERASE requests and redeems a private single-use confirmation token.
It erases local credentials and history, not server messages or backups.
